-- title:
--   A sandwich between the $2\ell$-shrinking, the $\ell$-shrinking and the set itself
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a normed additive commutative group, let $S \subseteq E$, let $\ell \ge 0$, and let $x, \xi \in E$ satisfy $\|\xi - x\| \le \ell$. Write $S[a] = \{\,y : y-a \in S\,\} = a + S$ for the translate of $S$ by $a$ and
--   $$S_r \;=\; \{\,y \in S : \bar B_r(y) \subseteq S\,\}$$
--   for the $r$-shrinking of $S$. Then
--   $$\bigl(S_{2\ell}\bigr)[\xi] \;\subseteq\; \bigl(S_{\ell}\bigr)[x] \qquad\text{and}\qquad \bigl(S_{\ell}\bigr)[x] \;\subseteq\; S[\xi] .$$
--
--   The two inclusions say that shrinking by $\ell$ absorbs a displacement of the base point by $\ell$, in both directions: a set shrunk twice as much and based at a perturbed point still sits inside the once-shrunk set based at the original point, which in turn sits inside the unshrunk set based at the perturbed point. Applied to a cone, this is what allows the base point of a cone condition to be moved anywhere within distance $\ell$ at the cost of one level of shrinking.
